{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790696080,"nonce":"ffOL3f9DPGSp/VILC5cuPrf5OqA=","title":"Generic member and iterator result types retain unbound class parameters","message":"The 755/1094 conformance baseline prints pointer values in Issue3535 and Issue10304. MIR passes an unresolved tag (0) to haxe_value_to_string_by_tag when formatting fields returned by their generic iterators.\n\nclass_method_return_type reads next()'s declaration without applying the iterator receiver's class arguments. Field inference likewise returns the declared field type without substitution. Method return substitution handles some containers but leaves anonymous and nested result types unresolved.\n\nThe authored GenericMemberTypes regression covers class fields, anonymous method results, nested generic return types, and class/anonymous iterator results instantiated with strings, integers and floats. It passes Haxe and fails the baseline Rayzor at the generic record return assertion.\n\nThe separate Issue3592 virtual generic method failure retains an unresolved tag inside a vtable target. Concrete member result typing alone does not specialize that target.","files":null}]}